docs {
  # imei-check — local API collection

  Point at a running server (`npm run dev`) and hit **Run** on any request.

  Every request carries assertions, so this collection is not just a set of examples — it is an
  executable check of the rules the service must never break:

  - an unknown TAC is `inconclusive`, never `pass`
  - no response ever contains the full 15-digit IMEI
  - every section carries `coverage`, `checked_at` and its evidence
  - `/readyz` never depends on a provider
  - a well-formed, authorised request returns 200 even when every section is `unavailable`
  - there is no top-level `clean` boolean, ever
  - nothing is charged for a section we could not answer
  - a retried `POST /v1/checks` returns the first response and does not charge twice

  ## Folders

  **Health** and **Internal** need nothing but `npm run dev`, against a server started with or
  without `DATABASE_URL`.

  **Against a server started WITHOUT `DATABASE_URL`** (the free offline tier), **Free tier** and
  **Meta** also need nothing — no key, no database. **Paid needs a database and 404s without one**:
  the routes are only registered when `services` exist (see `apps/api/src/app.ts`). That 404 means
  "start the server with DATABASE_URL", not "something is broken".

  **Against a server started WITH `DATABASE_URL`** — single-consumer mode — every route requires
  an `apiKey`, including **Free tier** and **Meta**: this service now runs as one seeded
  tenant/API key for a single caller, not a public free tier alongside a paid one. Set `apiKey` in
  the Local environment (it is declared as a secret var, so it is never written to the file) — run
  `npm run seed:dev` to get one.

  With `DATABASE_URL` set but no provider credentials configured, the **Paid** sections still pass
  every assertion — they come back `unavailable(provider_not_configured)` at zero cost. That is
  the point: the contract does not depend on a supplier being up. Nothing in **Paid** is ever
  charged either way — billing was removed entirely.

  Every request tagged `paid` needs `apiKey` unconditionally. `npm run api:test` runs everything
  else; `npm run api:test:paid` (with `BRUNO_API_KEY` set) runs the tagged ones. If your local
  server has `DATABASE_URL` set, export `BRUNO_API_KEY` before running `npm run api:test` too —
  otherwise the now-gated **Free tier**/**Meta** requests 401.

  Test IMEIs live in the **Local** environment as variables, so no request file contains a
  15-digit number. That is deliberate: `apps/api/test/sentinel.test.ts` greps the whole repo for
  them.
}
